  "title": "Ex 5.21 · a ≡ b (mod n) gives a³ ≡ b³ (mod n)",
  "prompt": "Let $a, b, n$ be integers with $n \\ge 1$. Prove that if $a \\equiv b \\pmod n$, then $a^3 \\equiv b^3 \\pmod n$, that is, $n \\mid (a^3 - b^3)$.",
  "answer_format": "A structured proof: let, case, expr and witness steps (notes optional). No final answer box.",
  "difficulty": 2,
