  "answer": "",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "a ≡ b (mod n) means n | (a − b), so a = nk + b for some integer k.",
    "Substitute into a³ − b³: the b³ terms cancel and every remaining term has a factor of n."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Since $n \\mid (a - b)$, $a = nk + b$ for some integer $k$.",
    "$a^3 - b^3 = (nk + b)^3 - b^3 = n^3k^3 + 3n^2k^2b + 3nkb^2 = n(n^2k^3 + 3nk^2b + 3kb^2)$.",
    "The bracket is an integer, so $n \\mid (a^3 - b^3)$. $\\blacksquare$"
  ],
  "reference": {
    "book": "hammack-bop3",
    "section": "Chapter 5 exercises, #21 (p. 136)",
    "note": "This exact exercise, restated in ProofLab's words. Uses Definition 5.1 (congruence)."
  },
